{{Quote|What-what is that?''"<br />"''It's the Death Star. It's a bad place, from an old war.|[[D-O]] and Rey|<ref name="TROS Date">''[[Star Wars: The Rise of Skywalker: The Visual Dictionary]]'' dates the events of [[Star Wars: Episode IX The Rise of Skywalker|''Star Wars'': Episode IX ''The Rise of Skywalker'']] to one [[Standard year|year]] after the events of [[Star Wars: Episode VII The Force Awakens|''Star Wars'': Episode VII ''The Force Awakens'']]. As ''[[Star Wars: Galactic Atlas]]'' dates the events of ''The Force Awakens'' to [[34 ABY]], the events of ''The Rise of Skywalker'' must occur in [[35 ABY]].</ref>}}
A portion of the '''Death Star ruins''' were located in the [[ocean]]s of the [[moon]] [[Kef Bir]] in the [[Endor system]]. After the [[DS-2 Death Star II Mobile Battle Station|second]] [[Death Star]] was destroyed in [[4 ABY]] during the [[Battle of Endor]], portions of the [[superweapon]], including the [[Emperor's Throne Room]] where he kept [[Emperor's wayfinder|his wayfinder]], fell onto Kef Bir.

In [[35 ABY]], the [[Jedi]] [[Rey Skywalker|Rey]] and her [[Resistance]] comrades [[Mission to Kef Bir|journeyed]] to the moon in search of a [[wayfinder]] that led to [[Cloning|resurrected]] [[Darth Sidious]]'s [[Sith Citadel|redoubt]] on the [[planet]] [[Exegol]] deep inside the [[Unknown Regions]]. There, she faced the [[Dark side of the Force|dark]] [[Knights of Ren|warrior]] and [[Supreme Leader]] of the [[First Order]] [[Ben Solo|Kylo Ren]] in their final duel, which resulted in him turning back to the [[light side of the Force]].

==Description==
[[File:DS2HangarWreckage-SWcom.png|thumb|left|250px|Two TIE fighters rest in the wreckage of one of the hangars.]]
After the [[superweapon]]'s destruction during the [[Battle of Endor]] in [[4 ABY]],<ref name="Galactic Atlas" /> parts of the [[DS-2 Death Star II Mobile Battle Station|second]] [[Death Star]] fell onto Kef Bir, including parts of the northern pole and the southern edge of the [[battle station]]'s [[superlaser]] lens concavity.<ref name="Episode IX" /> The remains of the [[Emperor's Throne Room]] were also part of the wreckage, including a vault in the Throne Room where [[Darth Sidious]] kept his [[Jedi artifact|Jedi]] and [[Sith artifact]]s. Over the years, the structure of the Death Star ruins was eroded and waterlogged by the [[ocean]], becoming deeply unstable.<ref name="TRoS VD">''[[Star Wars: The Rise of Skywalker: The Visual Dictionary]]''</ref>

When the survivors of [[Company 77]]&mdash;a [[company]] of [[First Order stormtrooper|stormtroopers]] who defected from the [[First Order]]&mdash;settled on Kef Bir, they salvaged [[Galactic Empire|Imperial]] technology to create the equipment that helped them survive on the [[moon]]'s harsh environment.<ref name="TRoS VD" />

==History==
===The Battle of Endor===
[[File:ThroneRoomWreckage-SWcom.png|thumb|right|250px|The remnants of the Imperial Throne Room]]
After a successful attack on the second Death Star's reactor during the battle of [[Endor]],<ref name="Episove VI">{{Film|VI}}</ref> the ruins of the destroyed battle station subsequently fell to the surface of the [[Water|ocean]] moon Kef Bir.<ref name="Episode IX" /> The [[Rebel Alliance Navy|Alliance Fleet]] had also set up [[tractor beam]]s and [[Deflector shield|shields]] to protect the forest moon from debris.<ref name="Endor Debris">{{Twitter|starwars|status/790904500768866304|Star Wars|quote=The Rebel Alliance fleet deployed shields and tractor beams to prevent Death Star 2's meteroric debris from devastating Endor's forest moon.|archivefile=File:SWTweetEndorDebris.png}}</ref>

===Return of the Sith===
[[File:Acme-ShadowyCorruption.png|thumb|left|250px|Rey faced a Force vision of a dark side phantasm identified as "Dark Rey" in the Death Star ruins.]]
In [[35 ABY]],<ref name="TROS Date" /> the [[Jedi]] [[Rey Skywalker|Rey]] came to Kef Bir and the ruins there during her [[Mission to Kef Bir|quest]] to find the [[Emperor's wayfinder]] that could lead her to the resurrected Darth Sidious' [[Sith Citadel|stronghold]] on the [[Unknown Regions]] [[planet]] of [[Exegol]]. Rey was faced by<ref name="Episode IX" /> a phantasm of the [[dark side of the Force]]<ref name="TLC">''[[Star Wars: The Lightsaber Collection]]''</ref> in the form of a [[Force vision]] of herself; the vision<ref name="Rey Bio Gallery">{{Databank|rey-biography-gallery|Rey Biography Gallery}}</ref> of the so-called "Dark Rey"<ref name="CtE9 Dark Rey">{{Topps|set=2018 Topps Star Wars Galactic Moments: Countdown to Episode IX|cardname=Dark Rey}}</ref> within the Emperor's old throne room<ref name="TLC" /> showed Rey a future version of herself who had embraced the dark side. All the same, Rey successfully located the [[wayfinder]]. Before she could take it and return to her companions, however, her adversary [[Ben Solo|Kylo Ren]] destroyed it.<ref name="Episode IX" />

The pair dueled atop the ruins. Ren became distracted, sensing the [[death]] of his mother, [[Leia Skywalker Organa Solo|Leia Organa]], allowing Rey to gain the advantage and stab him. Rey subsequently healed him and took his [[Kylo Ren's TIE whisper|TIE/wi modified interceptor]], leaving him stranded aboard the second Death Star's wreckage. Ren then spoke to a memory of his father, [[Han Solo]], and subsequently renounced the dark side, throwing [[Kylo Ren's lightsaber|his weapon]] into the surrounding ocean and reclaiming his former identity of Ben Solo. In order to escape the moon and accompany Rey during her [[Battle of Exegol|confrontation]] with Darth Sidious,<ref name="Episode IX" /> Solo procured a [[TIE scout]] [[starfighter]]<ref name="TROS EE">''[[Star Wars: The Rise of Skywalker: Expanded Edition]]''</ref> that had survived the Death Star's destruction, and piloted it out of the ruins and off of Kef Bir.<ref name="Episode IX" />

==Behind the scenes==
The Death Star ruins first appeared in the [[2019]] film [[Star Wars: Episode IX The Rise of Skywalker|''Star Wars'': Episode IX ''The Rise of Skywalker'']], the third and final installment of the ''[[Star Wars]]'' [[sequel trilogy]].<ref name="Episode IX" />

The 2019 novel ''[[Force Collector]]'' by [[Kevin Shinick]], which was part of the ''[[Journey to Star Wars: The Rise of Skywalker]]'' publishing line, originally featured the protagonist [[Karr Nuq Sin]]<ref name="Force Collector">''[[Force Collector]]''</ref> visiting the remains of the Death Star,<ref name="Matt Martin tweet">{{Twitter|missingwords|1221841340385783809|[[Matt Martin]]|quote=Revisiting the destroyed Death Star.|archivefile=File:MattMartin_ForceCollector_tweet.png|archiveurl=https://archive.is/mNuuE}}</ref> just as Rey did in Episode IX.<ref name="Episode IX" /> According to Shinick, he inadvertently wrote this similar journey into the first draft of the novel and was informed that aspect needed to be changed to avoid treading the same ground as ''The Rise of Skywalker'' about a year prior to the book's publication and film's premiere.<ref name="TarkinsTopShelf">{{WebCite|url=https://tarkinstopshelf.libsyn.com/episode-83-star-wars-force-collector-with-kevin-shinick|text=Episode 83: Star Wars: Force Collector with Kevin Shinick|date=2019-12-03|archivedate=20200105182824}} {{C|timestamp: 38:00}}</ref>

